    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present 61 Durrow Road, Kimmage, to the market, an exceptional two-bedroom, two-bathroom terraced property that has been tastefully renovated and thoughtfully extended to an exacting standard. \n\nFrom the moment you step inside, it is clear that considerable care and attention to detail has gone into creating this wonderful home. The property combines contemporary style, quality finishes and practical living space, resulting in a superb turnkey residence that is ready for its new owners to simply move in and enjoy.\n\nThe accommodation is bright, spacious and beautifully presented throughout, with a well-considered layout that makes excellent use of the available space. The property has been upgraded with modern living in mind, while maintaining a warm and inviting atmosphere.\n\nTo the rear is one of the home's most impressive features, a self-contained garden room, providing a highly versatile additional space. This could be ideally suited as a home office, studio, gym, guest accommodation or a quiet retreat away from the main house. The flexibility offered by this space is sure to appeal to those seeking a property that can adapt to their individual needs.\n\nThe rear garden is another particular highlight. South-facing and enjoying an excellent level of natural light, it provides a wonderful private outdoor space and is perfect for relaxing or entertaining.\n\nInternally, the property has been finished to a high specification, with a stylish and contemporary aesthetic evident throughout. The thoughtful extension has created a home that feels considerably more spacious than many properties of this type, while the carefully selected finishes add a sense of quality and sophistication.\n\nDurrow Road is a mature, family-friendly address ideally positioned close to a wealth of local amenities. Residents can enjoy nearby parks including Eamonn Ceannt Park, Brickfield Park and Lansdowne Valley Park, while Ashleaf Shopping Centre, SuperValu Sundrive, Crumlin Village and a variety of cafés, restaurants and everyday conveniences are all within easy reach. The area is exceptionally well connected, with frequent Dublin Bus services, both Red and Green Luas lines within walking distance, and the M50 reachable in around 15 minutes, making commuting throughout Dublin straightforward."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nLiving Area - 4.23m x 6.41m\n\n\nDining Area - 3.62m x 2.47m\n\n\nKitchen - 2.69m x 3.06m\n\n\nBathroom - 2.68m x 2.37m\n\n\nBedroom - 3.80m x 3.35m\n\n\nBedroom - 2.14m x 2.95m\n\n\nBathroom - 1.98m x 2.13m\n\n\nGarden Room - 4.15m x 3.69m\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Exceptional two-bedroom, two-bathroom terraced home</li><li> Tastefully renovated and thoughtfully extended</li><li> Finished to a high specification throughout</li><li> Bright and spacious accommodation</li><li> Self-contained garden room to the rear</li><li> Ideal home office, studio, gym or additional living space</li><li> Private south-facing rear garden</li><li> Excellent natural light throughout</li><li> Contemporary kitchen and stylish modern finishes</li><li> Turnkey condition — ready for immediate occupation</li><li> Well-proportioned bedrooms</li><li> Two modern bathrooms</li><li> Highly versatile accommodation</li><li> Excellent potential for working from home</li><li> Popular and mature residential location</li><li> Close to Eamonn Ceannt Park, Brickfield Park and Lansdowne Valley Park</li><li> Convenient to Ashleaf Shopping Centre and SuperValu Sundrive</li><li> Close to Crumlin Village, cafés, restaurants and local amenities</li><li> Excellent public transport connections</li><li> Walking distance to both Red and Green Luas lines</li><li> Frequent Dublin Bus services nearby</li><li> Easy access to the M50</li><li> Excellent connectivity to Dublin City Centre and surrounding suburbs</ul>"
